{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1790892773220,"sessionID":"ses_f067aa4e5ffevXywEi5R47GsUe","part":{"id":"prt_0f9870f5a001T27nb2zh3BK2Eb","messageID":"msg_0f986faa0001Sv76SpXInmddD1","sessionID":"ses_f067aa4e5ffevXywEi5R47GsUe","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1790892775528,"sessionID":"ses_f067aa4e5ffevXywEi5R47GsUe","part":{"id":"prt_0f9870f5f001bGiO1vykxANSB5","messageID":"msg_0f986faa0001Sv76SpXInmddD1","sessionID":"ses_f067aa4e5ffevXywEi5R47GsUe","type":"text","text":"Submission complete. The four claims about synchronous `Retrying` callback ordering in `tenacity/__init__.py` were answered with exact source citations:\n\n- **after_runs_on_accepted_success: false** — on an accepted success, `_post_retry_check_actions` queues only `rs.outcome.result()` and returns; `after` is queued only on the retry path.\n- **wait_computed_before_stop: true** — `_run_wait` (computing `upcoming_sleep`) is queued and executed before `_run_stop` (evaluating the stop predicate).\n- **before_sleep_runs_when_stopped: false** — when `stop_run_result` is truthy, only `retry_error_callback` or `exc_check` is queued before an early return; `before_sleep` is queued only in the continue-retrying branch.\n- **retry_error_callback_replaces_exhaustion_error: true** — the callback becomes the final action; `iter` returns its result and `Retrying.__call__` returns it directly, so no `RetryError` is raised.","time":{"start":1790892773215,"end":1790892775522}}}
